verdict:
APPROVED AS A NON-FORGEABLE PREREQUISITE PRODUCER AND CLASSIFIER, WITH ONE SHOULD-FIX (P1) AND NOTES. I found no path to a false whitelist pass. The checks are:
- the ambient non-CLOEXEC descriptors are real;
- every owned descriptor lies inside the scan range;
- the full spawn result is inspected even on a nonzero return;
- the PID has a single owner, with checked TERM/KILL and reap;
- stdio and status are exact;
- close errors are recorded or force a nonzero exit;
- unknown rights cleanup is flagged.
The classifier rejected all 47 of my independent bad cases. P1 can damage the evidence captured after a failure but cannot create a pass. This is source and host-detector evidence only: no Darwin spawn, descriptor-whitelist or runtime result.
